STM32CubeU5
###########

Origin:
   STMicroelectronics
   https://www.st.com/en/embedded-software/stm32cubeu5.html

Status:
   version 1.8.0

Purpose:
   STMicroelectronics official MCU package for STM32U5 series.

Description:
   This package is an extract of official STM32CubeU5 package written by STMicroelectronics.
   It is composed of STM32Cube hardware abstraction layer (HAL) and low layer (LL) plus a set
   of CMSIS headers files, one for each SoC in the STM32U5 series.

Dependencies:
    None.

URL:
   https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeU5

Commit:
   07b6fedf4b0670eb45d8806176bcc77167f42124

Maintained-by:
   External

License:
   BSD-3-Clause

License Link:
   https://opensource.org/licenses/BSD-3-Clause

Patch List:
   *Changes from official delivery:
    -dos2unix applied
    -trailing white spaces removed

   *Provision to enable hal & ll asserts added
    -Added stm32cube/stm32u5xx/drivers/include/stm32_assert.h
    -Removed unused stm32cube/stm32u5xx/drivers/include/stm32_assert_template.h

   *Fix to remove PAGESIZE definition which conflicts with POSIX
    Impacted files:
     drivers/include/Legacy/stm32_hal_legacy.h


   *Fix RNG Nist Compliance Values for stm32u535/545
     Fixes an issue in RNG peripheral registers on stm32u535/545: one value was missing
     and two values where not matching values from AN4230.
     Impacted files:
      stm32cube/stm32u5xx/soc/stm32u535xx.h
      stm32cube/stm32u5xx/soc/stm32u545xx.h
     Issue reference:
      https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeU5/issues/63
     See also:
      https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/hal_stm32/pull/355

   *Fix HAL_MDF_IRQHandler
      HAL_MDF_IRQHandler handles IRQ flags in an if {} else if {} condition.
      This causes interrupts to be handled once and only the first flag
      encountered in the condition, while there can be several flags raised.
     Impacted files:
       drivers/src/stm32u5xx_hal_mdf.c
     ST Internal Reference: HAL1-27843

   See release_note.html from STM32Cube
